{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"Let the original diameter of the pizza be \\(d\\) inches. Therefore, the original radius \\(r\\) is \\(\\frac{d}{2}\\) inches. The area \\(A\\) of the original pizza is given by the formula for the area of a circle:\n\\[\nA = \\pi \\left(\\frac{d}{2}\\right)^2 = \\pi \\frac{d^2}{4}\n\\]\n\nWhen the diameter increases by 2 inches, the new diameter is \\(d + 2\\) inches, and the new radius is \\(\\frac{d+2}{2}\\) inches. The area of the new pizza is:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{new}} = \\pi \\left(\\frac{d+2}{2}\\right)^2 = \\pi \\frac{(d+2)^2}{4}\n\\]\n\nAccording to the problem, the area of the new pizza is 44% greater than the area of the original pizza. This can be expressed as:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{new}} = A + 0.44A = 1.44A\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the expressions for \\(A\\) and \\(A_{\\text{new}}\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\pi \\frac{(d+2)^2}{4} = 1.44 \\pi \\frac{d^2}{4}\n\\]\n\nWe can cancel \\(\\pi\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) from both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n(d+2)^2 = 1.44d^2\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":904,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[10061,279,4024,23033,315,279,22502,387,17767,67,57758,14924,13,15277,11,279,4024,10578,17767,81,57758,374,1124,11520,37018,90,67,15170,17,11035,8,14924,13,576,3082,17767,32,57758,315,279,4024,22502,374,2661,553,279,14806,369,279,3082,315,264,12671,510,59,9640,32,284,1124,2493,1124,2359,11520,37018,90,67,15170,17,11035,1291,29776,17,284,1124,2493,1124,37018,90,67,61,17,15170,19,532,59,2533,4498,279,23033,12703,553,220,17,14924,11,279,501,23033,374,17767,67,488,220,17,57758,14924,11,323,279,501,10578,374,1124,11520,37018,90,67,10,17,15170,17,11035,8,14924,13,576,3082,315,279,501,22502,374,510,59,9640,32,15159,59,1318,90,931,3417,284,1124,2493,1124,2359,11520,37018,90,67,10,17,15170,17,11035,1291,29776,17,284,1124,2493,1124,37018,96065,67,10,17,29776,17,15170,19,532,59,2533,11190,311,279,3491,11,279