e_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,4498,279,23033,315,264,22502,12703,553,220,17,14924,11,279,3082,12703,553,400,19,19,59,4,12947,3555,572,279,3082,11,304,9334,14924,11,315,279,4024,22502,30,17399,697,4226,304,3793,315,57960,2493,12947,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhen the diameter of a pizza increases by 2 inches, the area increases by $44\\%$. What was the area, in square inches, of the original pizza? Express your answer in terms of $\\pi$.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5e2b4ea0a675087bc3d3b37754d209721f4811e1d1d784d842b6f299c3673e8b"},"seconds":19.510573148727417,"seed":538006914760032812,"stop":"eos","text":"Let the original diameter of the pizza be \\(d\\) inches. Therefore, the original radius \\(r\\) is \\(\\frac{d}{2}\\) inches. The area \\(A\\) of the original pizza is given by the formula for the area of a circle:\n\\[\nA = \\pi \\left(\\frac{d}{2}\\right)^2 = \\pi \\frac{d^2}{4}\n\\]\n\nWhen the diameter increases by 2 inches, the new diameter is \\(d + 2\\) inches, and the new radius is \\(\\frac{d+2}{2}\\) inches. The area of the new pizza is:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{new}} = \\pi \\left(\\frac{d+2}{2}\\right)^2 = \\pi \\frac{(d+2)^2}{4}\n\\]\n\nAccording to the problem, the area of the new pizza is 44% greater than the area of the original pizza. This can be expressed as:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{new}} = A + 0.44A = 1.44A\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the expressions for \\(A\\) and \\(A_{\\text{new}}\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\pi \\frac{(d+2)^2}{4} = 1.44 \\pi \\frac{d^2}{4}\n\\]\n\nWe can cancel \\(\\pi\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) from both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n(d+2)^2 = 1.44d^2\n\\]\n\nExpanding and simplifying the equation:\n\\[\nd^2 + 4d + 4 = 1.44d^2\n\\]\n\\[\n4d + 4 = 0.44d^2\n\\]\n\\[\n0.44d^2 - 4d - 4 = 0\n\\]\n\nTo make the equation easier to solve, we can multiply through by 25 to clear the decimal:\n\\[\n11d^2 - 100d - 100 = 0\n\\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\(d = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 11\\), \\(b = -100\\), and \\(c = -100\\):\n\\[\nd = \\frac{-(-100) \\pm \\sqrt{(-100)^2 - 4 \\cdot 11 \\cdot (-100)}}{2 \\cdot 11} = \\frac{100 \\pm \\sqrt{10000 + 4400}}{22} = \\frac{100 \\pm \\sqrt{14400}}{22} = \\frac{100 \\pm 120}{22}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two potential solutions:\n\\[\nd = \\frac{220}{22} = 10 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad d = \\frac{-20}{22} = -\\frac{10}{11}\n\\]\n\nSince the diameter cannot be negative, we have \\(d = 10\\). The original area \\(A\\) is:\n\\[\nA = \\pi \\frac{d^2}{4} = \\pi \\frac{10^2}{4} = \\pi \\frac{100}{4} = 25\\pi\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the original pizza is \\(\\boxed{25\\pi}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{25\\pi}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:436"}
